{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/391217-i-m-stuck-with-my-game-and-could-use-some-help","id":391217,"title":"I'm stuck with my game and could use some help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-03T03:52:21-08:00","id":391217,"title":"I'm stuck with my game and could use some help","content":"I'll post this here since my question is kinda general, even if the chronicle I'm talking about is a NWoD one.<br /> <br /> I might have written myself into a corner this time.<br /> <br /> I'm running a game which is a Hunter the Vigil game set in an &quot;Arabian Nights&quot; setting. The closest inspiration I can think of it the novel <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vathek\" target=\"_blank\">Vathek</a>. The players are relatively normal humas, if we exclude some demonblood powers or mystical elixirs. I use stuff from all the gamelines but, as far as the characters are concerned, they only have access to stuff from Hunter.<br /> <br /> The game it's been going on for a while but we've come to the inevitable moment when the players encounter their first Djinn. Long story short, the PCs have come to the ruins of a city destroyed by an eruption only to find an hidden temple under the volcano and, inside it, a giant Ifrit bound there by ancient sorcerers in order to serve as a living battery for the temple's mystical defenses. The players will eventually find that someone stole the usual Important Artifact from the temple (that actually made the volcano erupt as some sort of last resort trap) and it will develop further into other stages of the game that don't matter here, but I have to consider that the player might want to free the Ifrit.<br /> <br /> While I've made quite clear that Djinn are not something to underestimate or play with, this is the first time they really meet one, so they have no real frame of reference to deal with her. They might be wary, they might be willing to listen and, knowing them, there's a high chance they might want to release her from the imprisonment and, to be honest, if they express such desire I'd rather allow it than making it impossible &quot;because I say so&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now, the Ifrit naturally wants to be freed and will try to convince the players to do so, but <i>I have absolutely no idea </i>what she might offer in exchange. The easy answers are the classical wish, but it can be problematic for obvious reasons (I know, I know: I run such a game and I'm not yet prepared to deal with wishes. I'm the one to blame) or, taking a hint from the first Arabian Nights story featuring a Djinn, the entity simply express its gratitude by trying to smash its saviors. I'm more than happy to show them that Djinn have their own alien and dangerous morality, but it kinda feels like a dick move from my part. I have not discared any of those options, but I'm not sure if they are the right ones.<br /> <br /> So, as I always do when I'm stuck, I've come seeking help. Any ideas about how I could deal with this situation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-03-2015, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T04:08:00-08:00","id":391231,"title":"","content":"First off, good that you're not going to just block the players. I've played under STs that did that, always aggravating. So, good points right off the bat.<br /> <br /> Djinns might offer a wish, that's true, but there's a better option: knowledge. Djinns are incredibly wise and knowledgeable beings, with often millennia of experience (even if the last couple hundred of that has been spent trapped in a volcano temple). Good odds that anything the players come up against, the djinn has seen it before, and can offer amazingly insightful advice. Of course, as you pointed out, that doesn't necessarily mean it's <i>helpful</i> advice; djinn are not to be trusted. Thus, the advice can often be incomplete, twisted or geared towards achieving the djinns ends rather than the players. Like, for example, a monster might need blood to be drawn in/destroyed. The djinn might say it requires the blood of a certain lineage, which happens to be the same lineage that the priests who trapped it belong to (not that the players know that). Or blood from a person meeting certain characteristics, which happens to remove potential threats/irritations from the djinns path.<br /> <br /> Given that knowledge is usually something hunters are lacking, it'd be pretty tempting for the players to have a near-infinite source.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T04:08:23-08:00","id":391233,"title":"","content":"In the original tales the Djinn where not capable of cosmic wish-granting. They will be glad to be freed, and will regard who has done so as a friend and will offer to do something in return for them, but they are limited by their abilities, they cannot twist the world to change to suit any request.<br /> <br /> So, have clear what the capabilities of this Djinn actually are and let them get the gratitude of a task performed by the Djinn on their behalf if they decide to free it. No fuss.<br /> <br /> Also, long time no see, Cinder! I still remeber fondly your fan-made Hosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T12:25:45-08:00","id":391746,"title":"","content":"Long forgotten knowledge is always a valuable thing that can be offered if you're looking for a reward. Knowledge of where a capital was of a people known for great wealth in the gold/silver range as well as great amounts of other metals, as they lived in what was called at the time &quot;The Metal Mountains&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T02:42:47-08:00","id":392460,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for your help.<br /> <br /> Both forgotten knowledge and the promise to do a task for them are going to be really tempting for my players. I'll probably make the Djinn offer both, so they can decide what feels more interesting. Ancient informations about other supernatural being or that point to power and wealth (even if requires morally dubious actions to be obtained or might turn out to be a part of the Djinn's plan) or the chance to throw a Rank 4 Ifrit at a problem will surely make them consider about freeing the Djinn. If I can get some plot hooks out of that or showing them how dangerous the Djinn are, all the better.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/391217-i-m-stuck-with-my-game-and-could-use-some-help?p=391231#post391231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, good that you're not going to just block the players. I've played under STs that did that, always aggravating. So, good points right off the bat..</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. It's not always easy: I have a player who thought the best way to obtain something after a job was to storm into the Caliph's throne room, sword in hand, while screaming &quot;I want some gold!&quot; and attacking a prince, but I make a point to usually let them do what they want to do (and face the consequences)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/391217-i-m-stuck-with-my-game-and-could-use-some-help?p=391233#post391233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, long time no see, Cinder! I still remeber fondly your fan-made Hosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hello! I still lurk around here, it's just that between school and work, I don't have the time to write all the fan-made stuff I planned to do (including the Bat Host I'd <i>love</i> to finish), much to my chagrin. Most of the NWoD things I write nowadays are to be used in my game. Historical setting aside, it ranges from detailed rules and Numina for Djinn to all sort of Spirits, monsters and Relics, it's just not that interesting and a bit too specific to share.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-04-2015, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T09:36:45-08:00","id":392653,"title":"","content":"For context, the specific example I gave is an actual thing. The metal mountains, great amounts of gold and silver and so on. It was a country attacked on a pretext and depending on how you read the historical record, either every soul there put to the sword, or all the nobility killed and the remains of the populace enslaved. The destruction/looting/mining greatly helped finance a boom of growth of the Roman empire over 2000 years ago.<br /> <br /> So perfect if you want to do the double-cross of the information not being worth much for all that it is ancient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T11:33:06-08:00","id":392789,"title":"","content":"If I can give my 2 cents. For me feeing a djinn is ripe for some drama. Me. I'd offer the players a few supernatural powers. Free of charge upon the release of the Djinn, pull a mummy though and gave the powers weaken over time until they're gone. Give the players a reason to seek out the djinn and a refuel. Of course. It be a high price.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}